{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "density_modulated_return_v1",
  "intent": "Shift emphasis from tour closure to local structure to reduce the gap on clustered/grid instances where parent underperforms. Modulate parent return-distance term by (1 - 0.4*cluster_density) so dense regions naturally de-emphasize closure while sparse/uniform regions keep parent behavior. Add positive cluster_density weight (0.08) to prefer interior dense nodes, slightly raise linear regret to 0.15 (helps avoid costly corner traps in clustered), and soften spread penalty to 0.04 to stop over-penalizing grid corners with naturally low spread. Distance still dominates.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "return_aware"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    s = f['spread']\n    denom = (0.5 + nr) if (0.5 + nr) > 1e-9 else 1e-9\n    return -d + 0.25 * (1 + p) * (1 - 0.4 * cd) * rd + 0.15 * r + 0.1 * r / denom + 0.08 * cd - 0.04 * s",
  "source": "live_llm",
